p.src:
Every two-index tensor splits uniquely into $\begin{aligned}\Psi_{ij}
&=\Psi^{(S)}_{ij}+\Psi^{(A)}_{ij},\\
\Psi^{(S)}_{ij}
&=\frac12(\Psi_{ij}+\Psi_{ji}),\\
\Psi^{(A)}_{ij}
&=\frac12(\Psi_{ij}-\Psi_{ji}).
\end{aligned}$ The two pieces obey $\Psi^{(S)}_{ij}=\Psi^{(S)}_{ji},
\qquad
\Psi^{(A)}_{ij}=-\Psi^{(A)}_{ji}.$ Equation [eq:l10-tensor-transform] preserves each condition, so group transformations never mix the symmetric and antisymmetric sectors.

